{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Lift up [your eyes to the heavens, etc.]</b> From this verse the men of discernment learned that the soul of man endures, and their statement is true. Therefore the meaning of the verse is not so. Rather, 'the heavens' is the firmament and 'the earth' is the inhabited earth, and the salvation of HaShem and His faithfulness and His righteousness stand forever."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:57.273048442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}